# Stripe: official SDK, blocking adapter, virtual-thread offload

Talk to Stripe with the official **stripe-java** SDK (`StripeClient`), not a Quarkus REST client. Wrap `StripeClient` in an adapter. The adapter is **blocking**. That is the cost of the SDK; do not pretend the HTTP call is non-blocking.

Do **not** hardcode the secret key. Inject it from config (environment first).

## Thread policy

The adapter does **not** choose a thread. No `@RunOnVirtualThread`, no `@Blocking`, on the adapter.

`@RunOnVirtualThread` is **optional** and belongs on the **caller** (the JAX-RS resource method, or other entrypoint) **only when that caller would otherwise run on the event loop**. If the caller is already on a virtual thread, or is not on the event loop, call the adapter with no extra annotation.

Event-loop paths must **scale**. Do **not** offload Stripe with `@Blocking` or any other hop onto the capped OS worker pool. A blocking signature without `@RunOnVirtualThread` is the worker pool — that is not acceptable for Stripe.

A resource that needs the SDK result **cannot** stay a `Uni` event-loop method. Give it a concrete return type and `@RunOnVirtualThread`. Do not wrap the SDK in `Uni` on the event loop. Do not mix `@RunOnVirtualThread` with a `Uni` (or `CompletionStage` / `Multi`) return type.

Default `HttpURLConnection` can pin a carrier. Do not "fix" pinning with `@Blocking`.

## Example

```kotlin
@ApplicationScoped
class StripeClientProducer {
    @Produces
    @ApplicationScoped
    fun stripeClient(
        @ConfigProperty(name = "stripe.api-key") apiKey: String,
    ): StripeClient = StripeClient(apiKey)
}

@ApplicationScoped
class StripePaymentAdapter(
    private val stripeClient: StripeClient,
) {
    fun createPaymentIntent(params: PaymentIntentCreateParams): PaymentIntent =
        stripeClient.v1().paymentIntents().create(params)
}

@Path("/payments")
class PaymentResource(
    private val stripePaymentAdapter: StripePaymentAdapter,
) {
    @POST
    @RunOnVirtualThread
    fun create(request: CreatePaymentRequest): PaymentResponse {
        val intent = stripePaymentAdapter.createPaymentIntent(toParams(request))
        return PaymentResponse(intent.id)
    }
}
```

## Do not

```kotlin
@ApplicationScoped
class StripePaymentAdapter(
    private val stripeClient: StripeClient,
) {
    @RunOnVirtualThread
    fun createPaymentIntent(params: PaymentIntentCreateParams): PaymentIntent =
        stripeClient.v1().paymentIntents().create(params)
}

@Path("/payments")
class PaymentResource(
    private val stripePaymentAdapter: StripePaymentAdapter,
) {
    @POST
    @Blocking
    fun create(request: CreatePaymentRequest): PaymentResponse =
        PaymentResponse(stripePaymentAdapter.createPaymentIntent(toParams(request)).id)

    @POST
    @Path("reactive")
    fun createReactive(request: CreatePaymentRequest): Uni<PaymentResponse> =
        Uni.createFrom().item {
            PaymentResponse(stripePaymentAdapter.createPaymentIntent(toParams(request)).id)
        }
}
```
